        "original_id": "335b5190-e2bf-5a80-b2c9-98f34805340f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Battle of Gettysburg, Battle of Tarawa, Gettysburg Address cemetery consecration\n- Places: Gettysburg, Pennsylvania, Tarawa, Pennsylvania Route 134\n- Topics: American Civil War, Pacific Theater of World War II\n\nFacts:\n- The Battle of Gettysburg was fought on July 1–3, 1863, in and around Gettysburg, Pennsylvania, by Union and Confederate forces during the American Civil War.\n- Pennsylvania Route 134 was used during the 1863 Battle of Gettysburg for the procession to the cemetery consecration where the Gettysburg Address was delivered.\n- The Battle of Tarawa was fought on 20–23 November 1943 in the Pacific Theater of World War II.",
